          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R34-Pad2) : R34.2(2,passive) SW6.1(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R35-Pad2) : R35.2(2,passive) SW6.2(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the termination switches are enabled, the two supposedly isolated CAN buses are cross-coupled through the 120-ohm resistors instead of being terminated within each bus. This can cause common-mode faults, loss of bus isolation, and unreliable CAN communication.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D4", "D14", "D23"],
      "pins": ["D4.2", "D14.2", "D23.2"],
      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "The net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW contains only the anodes of D4, D14, and D23; it has no supply connection or driver in the netlist.",
      "expected": "A net named LED_3.3V_POWER_SW should be connected to +3V3 or an equivalent switched LED power rail so that the Ethernet/power status LEDs can be powered through their current-limit resistors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW : D14.2(A,passive) D23.2(A,passive) D4.2(A,passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "D4, D14, and D23 will remain dark because their anodes are floating. This does not damage the board, but it removes the intended Ethernet/power status indication.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files appear to contain connectivity deviations: the e-stop buffer U22 is miswired with its A input tied to GND instead of +3V3, the CAN termination switch network appears cross-connected between CAN0 and CAN1, and the LED_3.3V_POWER_SW net is left floating without a supply connection."
